;(Talk to Todd)
:A child stands alone by the sea and, for some reason, his young face looks rather familiar.
:'''Todd:''' There you are.
:'''Todd:''' I was just hanging out over at the {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|high elder statue}} and there was this guy, completely silent, who couldn't take his eyes off me. I thought he could be from the Ten-Lords Commission, so I snuck over here.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How did you turn into... this?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What in the world happened?
:'''Todd:''' ...
:'''Todd:''' Hehe, I just was a little sloppy with my experiment. An inevitable result.
:'''Todd:''' I thought I'd gained immortality, but unfortunately things were not that simple.
:'''Todd:''' My body, it keeps shrinking. My skin, muscles, organs... Indeed, I'm getting younger, you see, but this "youth" doesn't seem to have an off switch.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You're de-aging?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Kind of like the Vidyadhara tradition of hatching rebirth...
::'''Todd:''' Yes. But so far as I know, their "rebirths" have a limit.
:'''Todd:''' Test results indicate that this de-aging process seems to have no endpoint. It won't be long before I'm illiterate and won't be able to understand my own reports &mdash; which would seem no difference from regular dementia.
:'''Todd:''' In the end, I might even become an egg again, just like the Vidyadhara. Perhaps I could become a human embryo once again &mdash; I mean, I'm not Vidyadhara, am I?
:'''Todd:''' Ahh... Isn't it ironic? Don't you think?
:'''Todd:''' My wish came true &mdash; just not in the form I thought it would take. The oldest stories in human civilization are fables that take this line. Seems like they aren't just a cliche, after all.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What can I help you with?
::'''Todd:''' ...
::'''Todd:''' No no, no need this time. You've already done so much for me. More than my teachers and apprentices combined. And I don't want to bother anyone else anymore.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Do you want me to fetch a healer from the Alchemy Commission?
::Todd's little eyes lit up with a flash of arrogance that was beyond his years.
::'''Todd:''' That look in your eyes... Are you pitying me?
::'''Todd:''' Please, (Trailblazer). There really is no need for anything. Just coming to chat with me is cause enough for celebration.
----
----
:'''Todd:''' In this life I've been far better off than most people, who don't even know what they want, let alone how to get it. I became a published author, and I've taken on countless apprentices. I may have no children, but there are several of my students of whom I'm rather proud.
:'''Todd:''' Best of all, I lived to see the results of my research &mdash; despite it all turning into a nasty joke. But... Enough, that's enough for now. I'm satisfied.
:The child's cherub face seemed to be smaller yet again.
:'''Todd:''' ...Sorry. That was a lot to just dump on you.
:'''Todd:''' I just wanted to... say thanks to you, (Trailblazer), for being there for me right from the start.
